hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1217","Abdullah bin Hashim told us, Abdullah bin Numayr told us, Othman, who is Ibn Hakim, told us, Aamir bin Saad told me, about His father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came one day from Aliya and when he passed by the mosque of Banu Muawiyah, he entered and kneeled in it. We prayed two rak'ahs, and we prayed with him, and he prayed to his Lord for a long time, then he turned to us and said: “I asked my Lord for three things, and He gave me two, but withheld one from me. I asked my Lord not to destroy my nation with the Sunnah and He gave it to me, and I asked Him not to destroy my nation by drowning and He gave it to me, and I asked Him not to make Their violence among themselves, so He prevented it.”"
"1218","Saeed bin Yahya bin Saeed Al-Umayyad told us, my father told us, Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Raja Al-Ansari, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad bin Al-Hahad On the authority of Muadh bin Jabal, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out and I went out with him to seek him, asking everyone I passed by, and he said: He passed. Before, I passed by and found him praying, so I waited for him until he left, and he had prolonged the prayer, so I said: I have seen you for as long as I have seen you. I prayed it like this. He said: “I prayed a prayer of desire and awe. I asked God for three, and He gave me two and withheld one from me. I asked Him not to He will destroy my nation by drowning, so he gave it to me. I asked him not to overpower an enemy other than them, so he gave it to me. I asked him not to throw his share among them, so he responded. \"Ali\""
"1219","Muhammad bin Bashar and Abu Musa narrated to us, saying: Othman bin Omar, narrated to us Shu’bah, narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ja’far Al-Madani, he said: I heard Amara Ibn Khuzaymah narrates, on the authority of Uthman Ibn Hunaif: A blind man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Pray to God to grant me health. He said: “Indeed If you wish, I may delay that, and it is better, and if you wish, I may pray.” Abu Musa said, he said: So call him, and they said: So he ordered him to perform ablution, Bundar said: And he should do well, and they said: And he should pray two rak’ahs and supplicate with this. Supplication: “O God, I ask You and I turn to You through Your Prophet Muhammad, the Prophet of Mercy. O Muhammad, I have turned to You to my Lord in this need of mine.” Then it will be decided for me. Oh God, grant him his intercession on my behalf.” Abu Musa added: And he made my intercession on his behalf. He said: Then, as if he had yet doubted me: And he made my intercession on his behalf."
